{"k":"report","status":"success","summary":"Set the auto-refresh to 1m via the top-bar refresh control (it opened a menu of intervals; I picked \"1 minute\"), then opened Edit > Save dashboard, saw the drawer's \"Update default refresh value — Will make the current refresh the new default\" checkbox (this version's wording for the default-refresh option), ticked it (a \"Changes 1\" tab appeared and Save became enabled) and clicked Save — Grafana showed the \"Dashboard saved\" alert and the dashboard version went 3 → 4. Verification on a hard reload of the bare URL (no query params): the top bar refresh control reads \"1m\" (aria-label \"Choose refresh time interval with current interval 1 minute selected\"), the time range shows \"Last 6 hours\", and Grafana itself re-added refresh=1m to the URL on load, i.e. the value came from the saved default. However, in Edit > Settings > JSON Model the stored model shows the refresh as the TOP-LEVEL field \"refresh\": \"1m\" while \"timepicker\" is EMPTY (\"timepicker\": {}), NOT \"timepicker\": { \"refresh\": \"1m\" } as the instruction hypothesised — this Grafana version stores the default refresh at the top level, so the 1m interval IS persisted, just not inside timepicker. Rest of the stored model: \"time\": {\"from\": \"now-6h\", \"to\": \"now\"}, \"tags\": [\"bench\"], schemaVersion 40, panel titles 'fwgr73-n1 Notes' and 'fwgr73-n1 Availability'.","values":{"dashboard_uid":"ffz989fhtrqioa","dashboard_version_after_save":"4 (was 3)","topbar_refresh_button_text":"1m","topbar_refresh_button_aria_label":"Choose refresh time interval with current interval 1 minute selected","topbar_time_range":"Last 6 hours","json_model_refresh_top_level":"\"refresh\": \"1m\"","json_model_timepicker":"\"timepicker\": {}","json_model_schemaVersion":"40","save_confirmation":"Dashboard saved","url_after_bare_load":"http://127.0.0.1:3000/d/ffz989fhtrqioa/fwgr73-n1-bench-dashboard?from=now-6h&to=now&timezone=browser&refresh=1m","timepicker_refresh